WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.033
-Our next guest is a very funny
comedian who's about to kick off

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:06.133
her national "Ya Girl Done Made
It" stand-up tour.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.601
For ticket information,
go to mspatcomedy.com.

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.701
She also created and stars in
"The Ms. Pat Show."

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:13.934
The third season is streaming
now on BET+.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.834
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:20.067
-Get the [bleep] off me!

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:22.567
Oh, I know you ain't just
knocked me off this bed.

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:27.634
They got bugs down here,
and it stink.

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:31.467
It smell like old meat stuck in
my teeth.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:34.701
I'm calling my agent.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.767
'Cause my manager ain't managing
[bleep].

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:41.167
-In fairness, I'd just like to
say I'm a recovering alcoholic.

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:43.033
-Unh-unh, honey.
You done had three months

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:44.868
to use that alcoholic excuse.

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:47.501
You just [bleep] up.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:52.734
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Ms. Pat.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:54.400
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.400 --> 00:01:02.367
♪♪

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:10.267
♪♪

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:12.133
Welcome back, Ms. Pat.

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.734
-Oh, so happy to be back.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:16.834
-You know, last time you were
here, we were talking about how

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.200
thanks to your success and
everything going so well

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.200
for you that your husband
retired.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.534
-Yeah, and I told you he bought
a drone that he couldn't use.

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:26.968
-Yeah.
-Now he's recording the evening

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:29.067
news and waking up
like it's new news.

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:30.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.534
And he was like, "People got
killed today."

00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:34.567
I'm like, "No, that was
last night.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:37.033
Stop recording the evening news,
okay?"

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:39.734
-So he tapes the evening news
and watches it in the morning?

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:41.667
-'Cause he go to bed at 6:30.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:46.634
-So, it sounds like he may be
having trouble keeping busy?

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:48.868
-No, he ain't having trouble
keeping busy.

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:51.067
He went out and bought
three big dogs, Seth.

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:52.534
-Okay.
-Cane corsos.

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:54.434
And I'm like, "What are we going
to do with these big old dogs?"

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:56.534
I mean big dogs.
And he cooks for them.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:58.567
So, I walk in the house,
and he cooking chicken feet.

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:01.300
I'm like, "My mama used to love
chicken feet."

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.567
Because my mama didn't have no
front teeth and it was easy

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:05.033
for the feet to go in
and out her mouth.

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:08.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:10.300
-So, this is very helpful.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.868
If you're missing
two front teeth,

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:13.767
you want a chicken foot that'll
just go in and out.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.367
-Go in and out.
-Oh, that's helpful. Great.

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.634
-And I can say that
'cause she's dead

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:17.701
and she can't hear us.

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:19.834
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:22.033
-You got to be careful what you
say about Black mamas.

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.634
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.434
-And so, we got these three big
dogs, and I'm like,

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:27.567
"You just could've went out
and got kids.

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:29.767
You know, at least we could file
them on our income taxes."

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:31.267
-Yeah.

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:33.534
-And they from the same litter,
so they brothers and sisters.

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:35.367
-Here's a look at these dogs.
Look at these dogs.

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:36.901
These are big dogs. Alright.

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:39.400
-Oh, they're only 4 months old,
so they're going to get bigger.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.534
They're going to be fat
like the rest of my family.

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:42.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:45.267
And so, these dogs are so big,

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:47.100
and, like, one of them jumped in
the bed with me

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.300
and hit me upside the head.
I started having a flashback

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.667
like a belt was hitting me.

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:55.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:59.934
And I told my husband, like,
"These dogs require healthcare."

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:02.501
When I had a dog, you could tie
them up to the tree.

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:04.300
You can't tie a dog
up to the tree now.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.601
And these are some boujee dogs
too.

00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:09.934
You know, you put -- one of them
have a -- he won't go to sleep.

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:11.567
All night just pressing on
his toy.

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.501
So I walk in there.
And, you know, I'm a Black mama.

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:15.367
I talk to my kids
not like you do.

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:17.267
So I take the broom.

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:19.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:20.934
You do time-out.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:24.067
I take the broom and hit the
cage, "Shut your damn mouth!"

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:27.234
-How is that going?
Are they responding well?

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:29.434
-They're responding
like Black kids. "Yes, ma'am."

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:32.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.901
-But it's expensive to feed
them.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.868
-There's three of them.
A girl and two boys.

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:38.901
-What are their names?
-Zeus, Kong, and Sheba.

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:40.734
So, one of them done got in
heat.

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:42.067
But they brothers and sisters.

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.033
And you don't want the brother
to touch the sister.

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:45.501
But they don't know they
brothers and sisters.

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:49.067
So, he done put the dog on my
daughter panties.

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:50.868
And I'm like, "You don't think
this dog know

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.167
how to slide it to the side?"

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:57.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.534 --> 00:04:00.234
What man don't know
that old trick?

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:02.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:05.467
So now we got the dog running
around with girl panties on.

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:07.701
I'm like,
"That's not gonna help."

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:09.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:12.767
You're going to have to put on
a panty liner to keep her off.

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:15.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:17.767
-Did you have dogs growing up
when you were a kid?

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.501
-I had one dog named Pup-Pup.

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:21.334
And Ronald Reagan killed my dog.

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:22.734
-What?
Ronald Reagan killed your dog?

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:24.634
-Yeah. We Democrats,
so he got re-elected,

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:25.901
and the dog jumped out
the back porch.

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:30.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.334
That's why I'm a Democrat.

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:34.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:38.100
That's a true story.
-Oh, that's a true story?

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.400
Jumped out --
Like jumped off the porch?

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.667
-We was listening to
the election.

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.701
I'll never forget it,
on a little radio.

00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:45.767
And he said, "Your new president
is Ronald Reagan."

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:47.300
And my dog jumped out
the back porch.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:50.868
My dog was like,
"Y'all didn't have no Alpo

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:52.133
the first four years.

00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:53.634
I know y'all ain't going to have
none the next four."

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:55.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:57.634
-You're so busy.
I'm so impressed.

00:04:57.634 --> 00:05:00.234
You've got your show.
You've got your podcast.

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:01.734
-Yes.
-You've got radio.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.534
-Yes.
-You're going on tour.

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:06.200
But tell me, what's
your daily routine?

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.300
What time do you get started?

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.100
-I wake up every morning about
3:00.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.367
-Oh, my goodness.
-Because he snore like a horse.

00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:14.467
-Yeah.
-So I get up in the morning

00:05:14.467 --> 00:05:16.334
and I do TikTok.
I love TikTok.

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:17.300
-You love TikTok?
-Oh, I just --

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.033
[ Woman claps ]
Thank you, ma'am.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:21.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:24.667
TikTok will make you buy things
that you can't even fit.

00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:26.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.434
I'll be on there buying clothes
your size.

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:30.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:31.901
I'll be buying four sweaters.

00:05:31.901 --> 00:05:34.067
And I tell my girl to put
these sweaters together.

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:38.834
-So you're very susceptible to
advertising when you see it?

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:40.934
You just jump right in?

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:44.501
-I like buying things.
Like, I bought a $2,000 faucet

00:05:44.501 --> 00:05:48.100
'cause my husband bought
a thousand dollars worth of dog.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:50.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.133
But he don't think
I need the faucet.

00:05:52.133 --> 00:05:53.400
I'm like,
"You don't need the dog.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.100
Do you know how much cold water

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.734
is going to come out
of this faucet?"

00:05:56.734 --> 00:05:58.601
You know all my girlfriends are
going to come over like,

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:00.367
"Oh, my God, look at
this faucet."

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:02.567
I'm like, "Yeah, $2,200."

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:06.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:08.000
Hey, I'm a Black kid
from the hood.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.000
I got a little money now.
I don't know how to act.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.701
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:13.868
You got that faucet money.
-I bought two of them.

00:06:13.868 --> 00:06:15.934
-You bought two?
-Yeah, but my husband's asleep,

00:06:15.934 --> 00:06:17.133
so he ain't gonna see this show.

00:06:17.133 --> 00:06:20.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:26.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:29.300
-I know one of your dreams --
and, again, with everything

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.367
you've got going on right now,

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:31.701
I don't know where you'll find
the time.

00:06:31.701 --> 00:06:33.000
But you want to host
a game show.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.501
And you have a very good idea.

00:06:34.501 --> 00:06:38.767
-I want to host a newlywed game
but with grown people content.

00:06:38.767 --> 00:06:41.334
Like say, for instance,
I've been married 30 years.

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:42.968
And we bring the mother-in-law
on there.

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:45.100
Everybody got a mother-in-law
from hell, right?

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:47.067
-Yeah.
-So, I get to tell

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:49.901
my mother-in-law that she look
like James Brown.

00:06:49.901 --> 00:06:52.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.701 --> 00:06:55.968
She really do, and I was waiting
to tell her that, but she died.

00:06:55.968 --> 00:06:56.901
So --

00:06:56.901 --> 00:06:59.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:03.734
But imagine if you could really
tell your in-laws or tell people

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:06.033
off that are a part of
your husband family.

00:07:06.033 --> 00:07:08.267
And a lot of women
don't get to say it.

00:07:08.267 --> 00:07:10.300
Mother-in-laws are the devil.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:13.434
-So you didn't have a good
relationship with yours?

00:07:13.434 --> 00:07:16.167
-Not in the beginning.
Towards the end, she was okay.

00:07:16.167 --> 00:07:17.701
You know, I used to give her
my food stamps.

00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:19.868
And she still didn't like me.
-Really?

00:07:19.868 --> 00:07:21.300
-Until I cussed her out.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:24.434
I told her one day, "When you
help me sleep with this fat man,

00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:26.133
then you can tell me
what to do."

00:07:26.133 --> 00:07:29.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.501 --> 00:07:31.100
-How did she respond to that?

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:32.234
-She prayed.

00:07:32.234 --> 00:07:34.167
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.167 --> 00:07:36.400
She was a Christian,
and I don't like Christians.

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.601 --> 00:07:41.234
They pray too much
for unnecessary stuff.

00:07:41.234 --> 00:07:43.534
I don't want to hear that mess.
And God is busy.

00:07:43.534 --> 00:07:44.801
That's how we lost Betty White.

00:07:44.801 --> 00:07:46.234
They clogging up
the prayer line.

00:07:46.234 --> 00:07:48.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:50.100
-They were praying about
nonsense?

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:52.167
-Nonsense, Gucci belts, cars.

00:07:52.167 --> 00:07:53.601
And God killed Betty White.

00:07:53.601 --> 00:07:55.067
Forgot her birthday party
was coming up.

00:07:55.067 --> 00:07:56.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.634
I truly believe that.
-Congratulations.

00:07:57.634 --> 00:08:00.467
Season 3 of "The Ms. Pat Show."
-Season 3.

00:08:00.467 --> 00:08:01.701
-And you got to work with
Marla Gibbs,

00:08:01.701 --> 00:08:03.667
talking about an American legend
right there.

00:08:03.667 --> 00:08:05.267
-We got her to cuss.
-That's amazing.

00:08:05.267 --> 00:08:07.234
You got Marla Gibbs to --
-I'm going to get you to cuss.

00:08:07.234 --> 00:08:08.434
Come on over to BET+.

00:08:08.434 --> 00:08:10.334
-Oh, man. I'll tell you this.

00:08:10.334 --> 00:08:12.067
-He's an old man.
"I've never been there."

00:08:12.067 --> 00:08:14.501
-I will, I will -- I will do --
I would do an episode of

00:08:14.501 --> 00:08:15.968
"The Ms. Pat Show"
in a heartbeat.

00:08:15.968 --> 00:08:18.667
Get me one of those tiny beds,
and we'll have a fun old time.

00:08:18.667 --> 00:08:20.467
-I got -- You know it's
an all-white community.

00:08:20.467 --> 00:08:21.868
I got something for you.

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:23.501
-Yeah. Alright, great.
There we go.

00:08:23.501 --> 00:08:25.367
I'm a terrible actor,
but I would love to do it.

00:08:25.367 --> 00:08:28.167
-Before I get out of here, can I
please tell you my owl story?

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:30.133
-Yeah.
-So, my girlfriend live

00:08:30.133 --> 00:08:31.467
in the city of Atlanta.

00:08:31.467 --> 00:08:33.501
And I'm sitting in her yard
one night on the phone.

00:08:33.501 --> 00:08:34.601
You know, kind of in the hood

00:08:34.601 --> 00:08:36.167
where they sell drugs
down the street.

00:08:36.167 --> 00:08:37.400
And I'm just sitting there
on the phone.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.033
But all of a sudden,
this thing starts floating

00:08:39.033 --> 00:08:40.300
out of the air like Jesus.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:41.767
I'm like,
"What the hell is that?"

00:08:41.767 --> 00:08:44.434
I put on my bright light,
and it's a real owl.

00:08:44.434 --> 00:08:47.534
And he turned his head around
and his eyes glowed up.

00:08:47.534 --> 00:08:49.200
I said, "Oh, I don't mess
with nothing

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.634
that ain't got no damn neck."

00:08:50.634 --> 00:08:53.400
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.000
I put my car in reverse.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.334
I said, "Bitch, you got an owl
in your yard!"

00:08:57.334 --> 00:09:01.868
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.868 --> 00:09:04.067
It was the hood!
I never seen --

00:09:04.067 --> 00:09:06.100
Those type of animals don't come
to the hood.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.367
-Yeah.

00:09:07.367 --> 00:09:10.000
-We do pit bulls
and cane corsos.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:11.467
We don't do no damn owl!

00:09:11.467 --> 00:09:12.901
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.901 --> 00:09:14.767
And he was flying like Jesus.

00:09:14.767 --> 00:09:18.400
He hit that ground, I said,
"Hell to the no, no, no."

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:21.000
[ Laughter ]

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.501
-I'm very happy you shared
your owl story.

00:09:23.501 --> 00:09:25.033
[ Laughter ]

00:09:25.033 --> 00:09:26.868
-I've never seen him again
but I never --

00:09:26.868 --> 00:09:28.801
I don't go back to my friend
house at nighttime.

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:30.000
[ Laughter ]

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.300
Mnh-mnh. I don't know
where she --

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.300
I don't know how an owl
got to the hood.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:35.067
-Yeah. Well, it's probably
this Flaco one in Central Park.

00:09:35.067 --> 00:09:37.033
-No, he not Flaco.
He had a gold chain on.

00:09:37.033 --> 00:09:39.534
[ Laughter ]

00:09:39.534 --> 00:09:41.934
-That's the great Ms. Pat,
everybody.

00:09:41.934 --> 00:09:44.701
"Ms. Pat Show" streaming now on
BET+.

00:09:44.701 --> 00:09:48.000
For information on her tour --
